{"cells":[{"value":"# Homework 1\n## Dimensional Data Modeling - Week 1\n\nThis week's assignment involves working with the `actor_films` dataset. Your task is to construct a series of SQL queries and table definitions that will allow us to model the actor_films dataset in a way that facilitates efficient analysis. This involves creating new tables, defining data types, and writing queries to populate these tables with data from the actor_films dataset\n\n\n### Dataset Overview\nThe `actor_films` dataset contains the following fields:\n\n- `actor`: The name of the actor.\n- `actorid`: A unique identifier for each actor.\n- `film`: The name of the film.\n- `year`: The year the film was released.\n- `votes`: The number of votes the film received.\n- `rating`: The rating of the film.\n- `filmid`: A unique identifier for each film.\n\nThe primary key for this dataset is (`actor_id`, `film_id`).","kind":"sql","language":"sql"},{"value":"## 1. **DDL for `actors` table:** Create a DDL for an `actors` table with the following fields:\n\n- `films`: An array of `struct` with the following fields:\n\t- film: The name of the film.\n\t- votes: The number of votes the film received.\n\t- rating: The rating of the film.\n\t- filmid: A unique identifier for each film.\n\n- `quality_class`: This field represents an actor's performance quality, determined by the average rating of movies of their most recent year. It's categorized as follows:\n\t- `star`: Average rating > 8.\n\t- `good`: Average rating > 7 and ≤ 8.\n\t- `average`: Average rating > 6 and ≤ 7.\n\t- `bad`: Average rating ≤ 6.\n- `is_active`: A BOOLEAN field that indicates whether an actor is currently active in the film industry (i.e., making films this year).","kind":"sql","language":"sql"},{"value":"DROP TABLE actors;\nDROP TYPE IF EXISTS films;\nDROP TYPE IF EXISTS quality_class;","kind":"sql","language":"sql"},{"value":"CREATE TYPE films AS (\n    year INTEGER,\n    film TEXT,\n    votes INTEGER,\n    rating REAL,\n    filmid TEXT\n);\n\nCREATE TYPE quality_class AS\n    ENUM ('bad', 'average', 'good', 'star');\n\nCREATE TABLE actors (\n    actorid TEXT,\n    films films[],\n    quality_class quality_class,\n    is_active BOOLEAN,\n    current_year INTEGER,\n    PRIMARY KEY (actorid, current_year)\n);","kind":"sql","language":"sql"},{"value":"## 2. **Cumulative table generation query:** Write a query that populates the `actors` table one year at a time.","kind":"sql","language":"sql"},{"value":"-- First rows in actors table\nINSERT INTO actors\nWITH \nlast_year AS (\n    SELECT *\n    FROM actors \n    WHERE current_year = 1972 -- none data\n),\nthis_year AS (\n    SELECT\n    actorid,\n    year,\n    ARRAY_AGG(ROW(year,film, votes, rating, filmid)::films) as films,\n    AVG(rating) as avg_rating\n    FROM actor_films\n    WHERE year = 1973 -- 1st year of the actor\n    GROUP BY actorid, year\n)\nSELECT\n    COALESCE(ty.actorid, ly.actorid) as actorid,\n    CASE \n        WHEN ly.films IS NULL THEN ty.films\n        WHEN ty.year IS NOT NULL THEN ly.films ||ty.films\n        ELSE ly.films\n    END as films,\n    CASE\n        WHEN ty.avg_rating IS NULL THEN ly.quality_class\n        WHEN ty.avg_rating <= 6 THEN 'bad'\n        WHEN ty.avg_rating <= 7 THEN 'average'\n        WHEN ty.avg_rating <= 8 THEN 'good'\n        ELSE 'star'\n    END::quality_class AS quality_class,\n    CASE\n        WHEN ty.year IS NOT Null THEN true\n        ELSE False\n    END as is_active,\n    COALESCE(ty.year, ly.current_year+1) as current_year\nFROM \n    last_year as ly\nFULL OUTER JOIN \n    this_year as ty\n    ON ty.actorid = ly.actorid\n ;\n    ","kind":"sql","language":"sql"},{"value":"/*\n-- Unnest films\nWITH unnest AS(\n    SELECT actorid,\n         UNNEST(films) AS films-- CROSS JOIN UNNEST\n  FROM actors\n)\nSELECT actorid, (films).* FROM unnest;\n*/","kind":"sql","language":"sql"},{"value":"3. **DDL for `actors_history_scd` table:** Create a DDL for an `actors_history_scd` table with the following features:\n    - Implements type 2 dimension modeling (i.e., includes `start_date` and `end_date` fields).\n    - Tracks `quality_class` and `is_active` status for each actor in the `actors` table.\n     ","kind":"markdown","language":"markdown"},{"value":"WITH \nprevious AS(\nSELECT  \n    actorid,\n    current_year,\n    is_active,\n    quality_class,\n    LAG(is_active, 1) OVER (PARTITION BY actorid ORDER BY current_year) as previous_is_active,\n    LAG(quality_class, 1) OVER (PARTITION BY actorid ORDER BY current_year) as previous_quality_class\nFROM actors\n),\nindicators AS(\nSELECT \n    *,\n    CASE WHEN previous_is_active <> is_active THEN 1 \n    WHEN previous_quality_class <> quality_class THEN 1\n    ELSE 0 END as change_indicator\nFROM previous\n),\nstreaks AS(\nSELECT \n    *,\n    SUM(change_indicator) OVER (PARTITION BY actorid ORDER BY current_year) as streak_identifier\nFROM indicators\n)\nSELECT \n    actorid,\n    streak_identifier,\n    is_active,\n    quality_class,\n    MIN(current_year) AS start_year,\n    MAX(current_year) AS end_year\nFROM streaks\nGROUP BY actorid, streak_identifier, is_active, quality_class\nORDER BY actorid, start_year;","kind":"sql","language":"sql"}],"metadata":{"connectionId":"1750772779750","databaseName":"postgres","host":"localhost","port":5432,"username":"postgres","custom":{"cells":[{"value":"# Homework 1\n## Dimensional Data Modeling - Week 1\n\nThis week's assignment involves working with the `actor_films` dataset. Your task is to construct a series of SQL queries and table definitions that will allow us to model the actor_films dataset in a way that facilitates efficient analysis. This involves creating new tables, defining data types, and writing queries to populate these tables with data from the actor_films dataset\n\n\n### Dataset Overview\nThe `actor_films` dataset contains the following fields:\n\n- `actor`: The name of the actor.\n- `actorid`: A unique identifier for each actor.\n- `film`: The name of the film.\n- `year`: The year the film was released.\n- `votes`: The number of votes the film received.\n- `rating`: The rating of the film.\n- `filmid`: A unique identifier for each film.\n\nThe primary key for this dataset is (`actor_id`, `film_id`).","kind":"sql","language":"sql"},{"value":"## 1. **DDL for `actors` table:** Create a DDL for an `actors` table with the following fields:\n\n- `films`: An array of `struct` with the following fields:\n\t- film: The name of the film.\n\t- votes: The number of votes the film received.\n\t- rating: The rating of the film.\n\t- filmid: A unique identifier for each film.\n\n- `quality_class`: This field represents an actor's performance quality, determined by the average rating of movies of their most recent year. It's categorized as follows:\n\t- `star`: Average rating > 8.\n\t- `good`: Average rating > 7 and ≤ 8.\n\t- `average`: Average rating > 6 and ≤ 7.\n\t- `bad`: Average rating ≤ 6.\n- `is_active`: A BOOLEAN field that indicates whether an actor is currently active in the film industry (i.e., making films this year).","kind":"sql","language":"sql"},{"value":"DROP TABLE actors;\nDROP TYPE IF EXISTS films;\nDROP TYPE IF EXISTS quality_class;","kind":"sql","language":"sql"},{"value":"CREATE TYPE films AS (\n    year INTEGER,\n    film TEXT,\n    votes INTEGER,\n    rating REAL,\n    filmid TEXT\n);\n\nCREATE TYPE quality_class AS\n    ENUM ('bad', 'average', 'good', 'star');\n\nCREATE TABLE actors (\n    actorid TEXT,\n    films films[],\n    quality_class quality_class,\n    is_active BOOLEAN,\n    current_year INTEGER,\n    PRIMARY KEY (actorid, current_year)\n);","kind":"sql","language":"sql"},{"value":"## 2. **Cumulative table generation query:** Write a query that populates the `actors` table one year at a time.","kind":"sql","language":"sql"},{"value":"-- First rows in actors table\nINSERT INTO actors\nWITH \nlast_year AS (\n    SELECT *\n    FROM actors \n    WHERE current_year = 1972 -- none data\n),\nthis_year AS (\n    SELECT\n    actorid,\n    year,\n    ARRAY_AGG(ROW(year,film, votes, rating, filmid)::films) as films,\n    AVG(rating) as avg_rating\n    FROM actor_films\n    WHERE year = 1973 -- 1st year of the actor\n    GROUP BY actorid, year\n)\nSELECT\n    COALESCE(ty.actorid, ly.actorid) as actorid,\n    CASE \n        WHEN ly.films IS NULL THEN ty.films\n        WHEN ty.year IS NOT NULL THEN ly.films ||ty.films\n        ELSE ly.films\n    END as films,\n    CASE\n        WHEN ty.avg_rating IS NULL THEN ly.quality_class\n        WHEN ty.avg_rating <= 6 THEN 'bad'\n        WHEN ty.avg_rating <= 7 THEN 'average'\n        WHEN ty.avg_rating <= 8 THEN 'good'\n        ELSE 'star'\n    END::quality_class AS quality_class,\n    CASE\n        WHEN ty.year IS NOT Null THEN true\n        ELSE False\n    END as is_active,\n    COALESCE(ty.year, ly.current_year+1) as current_year\nFROM \n    last_year as ly\nFULL OUTER JOIN \n    this_year as ty\n    ON ty.actorid = ly.actorid\n ;\n    ","kind":"sql","language":"sql"},{"value":"/*\n-- Unnest films\nWITH unnest AS(\n    SELECT actorid,\n         UNNEST(films) AS films-- CROSS JOIN UNNEST\n  FROM actors\n)\nSELECT actorid, (films).* FROM unnest;\n*/","kind":"sql","language":"sql"},{"value":"3. **DDL for `actors_history_scd` table:** Create a DDL for an `actors_history_scd` table with the following features:\n    - Implements type 2 dimension modeling (i.e., includes `start_date` and `end_date` fields).\n    - Tracks `quality_class` and `is_active` status for each actor in the `actors` table.\n     ","kind":"markdown","language":"markdown"},{"value":"WITH \nprevious AS(\nSELECT  \n    actorid,\n    current_year,\n    is_active,\n    quality_class,\n    LAG(is_active, 1) OVER (PARTITION BY actorid ORDER BY current_year) as previous_is_active,\n    LAG(quality_class, 1) OVER (PARTITION BY actorid ORDER BY current_year) as previous_quality_class\nFROM actors\n),\nindicators AS(\nSELECT \n    *,\n    CASE WHEN previous_is_active <> is_active THEN 1 \n    WHEN previous_quality_class <> quality_class THEN 1\n    ELSE 0 END as change_indicator\nFROM previous\n),\nstreaks AS(\nSELECT \n    *,\n    SUM(change_indicator) OVER (PARTITION BY actorid ORDER BY current_year) as streak_identifier\nFROM indicators\n)\nSELECT \n    actorid,\n    streak_identifier,\n    is_active,\n    quality_class,\n    MIN(current_year) AS start_year,\n    MAX(current_year) AS end_year\nFROM streaks\nGROUP BY actorid, streak_identifier, is_active, quality_class\nORDER BY actorid, start_year;","kind":"sql","language":"sql"}],"metadata":{"connectionId":"1750772779750","databaseName":"postgres","host":"localhost","port":5432,"username":"postgres","custom":{"cells":[],"metadata":{"connectionId":"1750772779750","databaseName":"postgres","host":"localhost","port":5432,"username":"postgres","custom":{"cells":[{"value":"# Homework 1\n## Dimensional Data Modeling - Week 1\n\nThis week's assignment involves working with the `actor_films` dataset. Your task is to construct a series of SQL queries and table definitions that will allow us to model the actor_films dataset in a way that facilitates efficient analysis. This involves creating new tables, defining data types, and writing queries to populate these tables with data from the actor_films dataset\n\n\n### Dataset Overview\nThe `actor_films` dataset contains the following fields:\n\n- `actor`: The name of the actor.\n- `actorid`: A unique identifier for each actor.\n- `film`: The name of the film.\n- `year`: The year the film was released.\n- `votes`: The number of votes the film received.\n- `rating`: The rating of the film.\n- `filmid`: A unique identifier for each film.\n\nThe primary key for this dataset is (`actor_id`, `film_id`).","kind":"markdown","language":"markdown"},{"value":"## 1. **DDL for `actors` table:** Create a DDL for an `actors` table with the following fields:\n\n- `films`: An array of `struct` with the following fields:\n\t- film: The name of the film.\n\t- votes: The number of votes the film received.\n\t- rating: The rating of the film.\n\t- filmid: A unique identifier for each film.\n\n- `quality_class`: This field represents an actor's performance quality, determined by the average rating of movies of their most recent year. It's categorized as follows:\n\t- `star`: Average rating > 8.\n\t- `good`: Average rating > 7 and ≤ 8.\n\t- `average`: Average rating > 6 and ≤ 7.\n\t- `bad`: Average rating ≤ 6.\n- `is_active`: A BOOLEAN field that indicates whether an actor is currently active in the film industry (i.e., making films this year).","kind":"markdown","language":"markdown"},{"value":"DROP TABLE actors;\nDROP TYPE IF EXISTS films;\nDROP TYPE IF EXISTS quality_class;","kind":"sql","language":"sql"},{"value":"CREATE TYPE films AS (\n    year INTEGER,\n    film TEXT,\n    votes INTEGER,\n    rating REAL,\n    filmid TEXT\n);\n\nCREATE TYPE quality_class AS\n    ENUM ('bad', 'average', 'good', 'star');\n\nCREATE TABLE actors (\n    actorid TEXT,\n    films films[],\n    quality_class quality_class,\n    is_active BOOLEAN,\n    current_year INTEGER,\n    PRIMARY KEY (actorid, current_year)\n);","kind":"sql","language":"sql"},{"value":"## 2. **Cumulative table generation query:** Write a query that populates the `actors` table one year at a time.","kind":"sql","language":"sql"},{"value":"-- First rows in actors table\nINSERT INTO actors\nWITH \nlast_year AS (\n    SELECT *\n    FROM actors \n    WHERE current_year = 1970 -- none data\n),\nthis_year AS (\n    SELECT\n    actorid,\n    year,\n    ARRAY_AGG(ROW(year,film, votes, rating, filmid)::films) as films,\n    AVG(rating) as avg_rating\n    FROM actor_films\n    WHERE year = 1971 -- 1st year of the actor\n    GROUP BY actorid, year\n)\nSELECT\n    COALESCE(ty.actorid, ly.actorid) as actorid,\n    CASE \n        WHEN ly.films IS NULL THEN ty.films\n        WHEN ty.year IS NOT NULL THEN ly.films ||ty.films\n        ELSE ly.films\n    END as films,\n    CASE\n        WHEN ty.avg_rating <= 6 THEN 'bad'\n        WHEN ty.avg_rating <= 7 THEN 'average'\n        WHEN ty.avg_rating <= 8 THEN 'good'\n        ELSE 'star'\n    END::quality_class AS quality_class,\n    CASE\n        WHEN ty.year IS NOT Null THEN true\n        ELSE False\n    END as is_active,\n    COALESCE(ty.year, ly.current_year+1) as current_year\nFROM \n    last_year as ly\nFULL OUTER JOIN \n    this_year as ty\n    ON ty.actorid = ly.actorid\n ;\n    ","kind":"sql","language":"sql"},{"value":"/*\n-- Unnest films\nWITH unnest AS(\n    SELECT actorid,\n         UNNEST(films) AS films-- CROSS JOIN UNNEST\n  FROM actors\n)\nSELECT actorid, (films).* FROM unnest;\n*/","kind":"sql","language":"sql"},{"value":"SELECT * FROM actors WHERE is_active=false;","kind":"sql","language":"sql"},{"value":"","kind":"sql","language":"sql"}],"metadata":{"connectionId":"1750772779750","databaseName":"postgres","host":"localhost","port":5432,"username":"postgres","custom":{"cells":[],"metadata":{"connectionId":"1750772779750","databaseName":"postgres","host":"localhost","port":5432,"username":"postgres","custom":{"cells":[{"value":"# Homework 1\n## Dimensional Data Modeling - Week 1\n\nThis week's assignment involves working with the `actor_films` dataset. Your task is to construct a series of SQL queries and table definitions that will allow us to model the actor_films dataset in a way that facilitates efficient analysis. This involves creating new tables, defining data types, and writing queries to populate these tables with data from the actor_films dataset\n\n\n### Dataset Overview\nThe `actor_films` dataset contains the following fields:\n\n- `actor`: The name of the actor.\n- `actorid`: A unique identifier for each actor.\n- `film`: The name of the film.\n- `year`: The year the film was released.\n- `votes`: The number of votes the film received.\n- `rating`: The rating of the film.\n- `filmid`: A unique identifier for each film.\n\nThe primary key for this dataset is (`actor_id`, `film_id`).","kind":"markdown","language":"markdown"},{"value":"## 1. **DDL for `actors` table:** Create a DDL for an `actors` table with the following fields:\n\n- `films`: An array of `struct` with the following fields:\n\t- film: The name of the film.\n\t- votes: The number of votes the film received.\n\t- rating: The rating of the film.\n\t- filmid: A unique identifier for each film.\n\n- `quality_class`: This field represents an actor's performance quality, determined by the average rating of movies of their most recent year. It's categorized as follows:\n\t- `star`: Average rating > 8.\n\t- `good`: Average rating > 7 and ≤ 8.\n\t- `average`: Average rating > 6 and ≤ 7.\n\t- `bad`: Average rating ≤ 6.\n- `is_active`: A BOOLEAN field that indicates whether an actor is currently active in the film industry (i.e., making films this year).","kind":"markdown","language":"markdown"},{"value":"DROP TABLE actors;\nDROP TYPE IF EXISTS films;\nDROP TYPE IF EXISTS quality_class;","kind":"sql","language":"sql"},{"value":"CREATE TYPE films AS (\n    year INTEGER,\n    film TEXT,\n    votes INTEGER,\n    rating REAL,\n    filmid TEXT\n);\n\nCREATE TYPE quality_class AS\n    ENUM ('bad', 'average', 'good', 'star');\n\nCREATE TABLE actors (\n    actorid TEXT,\n    films films[],\n    quality_class quality_class,\n    is_active BOOLEAN,\n    current_year INTEGER,\n    PRIMARY KEY (actorid, current_year)\n);","kind":"sql","language":"sql"},{"value":"## 2. **Cumulative table generation query:** Write a query that populates the `actors` table one year at a time.","kind":"markdown","language":"markdown"},{"value":"-- First rows in actors table\nINSERT INTO actors\nWITH \nlast_year AS (\n    SELECT *\n    FROM actors \n    WHERE current_year = 1969 -- none data\n),\nthis_year AS (\n    SELECT\n    actorid,\n    year,\n    ARRAY_AGG(ROW(year,film, votes, rating, filmid)::films) as films\n    FROM actor_films\n    WHERE year = 1970 -- 1st year of the actor\n    GROUP BY actorid, year\n)\nSELECT\n    COALESCE(ty.actorid, ly.actorid) as actorid,\n    CASE \n        WHEN ly.films IS NULL THEN ty.films\n        WHEN ty.year IS NOT NULL THEN ly.films ||ty.films\n        ELSE ly.films\n    END as films,\n    Null::quality_class AS quality_class,\n    Null::boolean AS is_active,\n    COALESCE(ty.year, ly.current_year+1)::integer as current_year\nFROM \n    last_year as ly\nFULL OUTER JOIN \n    this_year as ty\n    ON ty.actorid = ly.actorid\n ;\n    ","kind":"sql","language":"sql"},{"value":"SELECT * FROM actors;","kind":"sql","language":"sql"}],"metadata":{"connectionId":"1750772779750","databaseName":"postgres","host":"localhost","port":5432,"username":"postgres","custom":{"cells":[],"metadata":{"connectionId":"1750772779750","databaseName":"postgres","host":"localhost","port":5432,"username":"postgres","custom":{"cells":[{"value":"# Homework 1\n## Dimensional Data Modeling - Week 1\n\nThis week's assignment involves working with the `actor_films` dataset. Your task is to construct a series of SQL queries and table definitions that will allow us to model the actor_films dataset in a way that facilitates efficient analysis. This involves creating new tables, defining data types, and writing queries to populate these tables with data from the actor_films dataset\n\n\n### Dataset Overview\nThe `actor_films` dataset contains the following fields:\n\n- `actor`: The name of the actor.\n- `actorid`: A unique identifier for each actor.\n- `film`: The name of the film.\n- `year`: The year the film was released.\n- `votes`: The number of votes the film received.\n- `rating`: The rating of the film.\n- `filmid`: A unique identifier for each film.\n\nThe primary key for this dataset is (`actor_id`, `film_id`).","kind":"markdown","language":"markdown"},{"value":"SELECT * FROM actor_films\nWHERE actorid = 'nm0000001'\nORDER BY year DESC;","kind":"sql","language":"sql"},{"value":"## 1. **DDL for `actors` table:** Create a DDL for an `actors` table with the following fields:\n\n- `films`: An array of `struct` with the following fields:\n\t- film: The name of the film.\n\t- votes: The number of votes the film received.\n\t- rating: The rating of the film.\n\t- filmid: A unique identifier for each film.\n\n- `quality_class`: This field represents an actor's performance quality, determined by the average rating of movies of their most recent year. It's categorized as follows:\n\t- `star`: Average rating > 8.\n\t- `good`: Average rating > 7 and ≤ 8.\n\t- `average`: Average rating > 6 and ≤ 7.\n\t- `bad`: Average rating ≤ 6.\n- `is_active`: A BOOLEAN field that indicates whether an actor is currently active in the film industry (i.e., making films this year).","kind":"markdown","language":"markdown"},{"value":"DROP TABLE actors;\nDROP TYPE IF EXISTS films;\nDROP TYPE IF EXISTS quality_class;","kind":"sql","language":"sql"},{"value":"CREATE TYPE films AS (\n    film TEXT,\n    votes INTEGER,\n    rating REAL,\n    filmid TEXT\n);\n\nCREATE TYPE quality_class AS\n    ENUM ('bad', 'average', 'good', 'star');\n\nCREATE TABLE actors (\n    actorid TEXT,\n    year INTEGER,\n    films films[],\n    quality_class quality_class,\n    is_active BOOLEAN,\n    PRIMARY KEY (actorid, year)\n);","kind":"sql","language":"sql"},{"value":"## 2. **Cumulative table generation query:** Write a query that populates the `actors` table one year at a time.","kind":"markdown","language":"markdown"},{"value":"SELECT year, count(*) FROM actor_films\nGROUP BY year\nORDER BY year\n\nLIMIT 1;","kind":"sql","language":"sql"},{"value":"WITH \nyesterar AS (\n    SELECT * FROM actors \n    WHERE year = 1969\n),\ntoday AS (\n    SELECT * FROM actor_films\n    WHERE year = 1970\n)\n\nSELECT\n    COALESCE(y.actorid, t.actorid) as actorid,\n    COALESCE(y.year, t.year) as year,\n    CASE \n    WHEN y.films IS NULL \n        THEN ARRAY[t.film, t.votes, t.rating, t.filmid]::films\n        ELSE y.films\n    END as films,\n    CASE\n        WHEN y.year IS NULL THEN t.quality_class\n        ELSE y.quality_class\n    END as quality_class,\nFROM \n    yesterar as y\nFULL OUTER JOIN \n    today as t\n    ON t.actorid = y.actorid;","kind":"sql","language":"sql"},{"value":"DELETE films;","kind":"sql","language":"sql"},{"value":"DELETE films;","kind":"sql","language":"sql"},{"value":"DELETE films;","kind":"sql","language":"sql"},{"value":"DELETE films;","kind":"sql","language":"sql"},{"value":"DELETE films;","kind":"sql","language":"sql"}],"metadata":{"connectionId":"1750772779750","databaseName":"postgres","host":"localhost","port":5432,"username":"postgres","custom":{"cells":[],"metadata":{"connectionId":"1750772779750","databaseName":"postgres","host":"localhost","port":5432,"username":"postgres","custom":{"cells":[{"value":"# Homework 1\n## Dimensional Data Modeling - Week 1\n\nThis week's assignment involves working with the `actor_films` dataset. Your task is to construct a series of SQL queries and table definitions that will allow us to model the actor_films dataset in a way that facilitates efficient analysis. This involves creating new tables, defining data types, and writing queries to populate these tables with data from the actor_films dataset\n\n\n### Dataset Overview\nThe `actor_films` dataset contains the following fields:\n\n- `actor`: The name of the actor.\n- `actorid`: A unique identifier for each actor.\n- `film`: The name of the film.\n- `year`: The year the film was released.\n- `votes`: The number of votes the film received.\n- `rating`: The rating of the film.\n- `filmid`: A unique identifier for each film.\n\nThe primary key for this dataset is (`actor_id`, `film_id`).","kind":"markdown","language":"markdown"},{"value":"SELECT * FROM actor_films\nWHERE actorid = 'nm0000001'\nORDER BY year DESC;","kind":"sql","language":"sql"},{"value":"## 1. **DDL for `actors` table:** Create a DDL for an `actors` table with the following fields:\n\n- `films`: An array of `struct` with the following fields:\n\t- film: The name of the film.\n\t- votes: The number of votes the film received.\n\t- rating: The rating of the film.\n\t- filmid: A unique identifier for each film.\n\n- `quality_class`: This field represents an actor's performance quality, determined by the average rating of movies of their most recent year. It's categorized as follows:\n\t- `star`: Average rating > 8.\n\t- `good`: Average rating > 7 and ≤ 8.\n\t- `average`: Average rating > 6 and ≤ 7.\n\t- `bad`: Average rating ≤ 6.\n- `is_active`: A BOOLEAN field that indicates whether an actor is currently active in the film industry (i.e., making films this year).","kind":"markdown","language":"markdown"},{"value":"-- Exercise 1\nCREATE TYPE films AS (\n    film TEXT,\n    votes INTEGER,\n    rating REAL,\n    filmid TEXT\n);\n\n CREATE TYPE quality_class AS\n     ENUM ('bad', 'average', 'good', 'star');\n    \n CREATE TABLE actors (\n    actorid TEXT,\n    films films[],\n    quality_class quality_class,\n    is_active BOOLEAN,\n    PRIMARY KEY (actorid)\n );\n","kind":"sql","language":"sql"},{"value":"## 2. **Cumulative table generation query:** Write a query that populates the `actors` table one year at a time.","kind":"markdown","language":"markdown"},{"value":"","kind":"sql","language":"sql"}],"metadata":{"connectionId":"1750772779750","databaseName":"postgres","host":"localhost","port":5432,"username":"postgres","custom":{"cells":[],"metadata":{"connectionId":"1750772779750","databaseName":"postgres","host":"localhost","port":5432,"username":"postgres","custom":{"cells":[{"value":"-- Connected to database: postgres\n-- Write your SQL query here\nSELECT * FROM actor_films\nLIMIT 100;","kind":"sql","language":"sql"}],"metadata":{"connectionId":"1750772779750","databaseName":"postgres","host":"localhost","port":5432,"username":"postgres","custom":{"cells":[],"metadata":{"connectionId":"1750772779750","databaseName":"postgres","host":"localhost","port":5432,"username":"postgres","enableScripts":true}},"enableScripts":true}},"enableScripts":true}},"enableScripts":true}},"enableScripts":true}},"enableScripts":true}},"enableScripts":true}},"enableScripts":true}},"enableScripts":true}},"enableScripts":true}},"enableScripts":true}},"enableScripts":true}}}}
